    {
      &quot;@id&quot;: &quot;https://www.nidads.com/blog/big-data-course-2026#faq&quot;,
      &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;FAQPage&quot;,
      &quot;mainEntity&quot;: [
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Do I need a computer science degree for a big data course?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Not really. Most programs just expect you to already know basic programming and SQL. Commerce, statistics, and engineering backgrounds all get accepted once you can show you have the core skills down.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;What salary can a fresher expect as a big data engineer in India?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Somewhere between ₹4 LPA and ₹8 LPA to start, moving toward the broader market average of ₹8.8–9.7 LPA within a year or two.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Is Hadoop still worth learning, or should I go straight to Spark?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Hadoop fundamentals still hold up — HDFS and YARN underpin most Spark clusters even today. But if you're starting fresh, put your energy into Spark and a cloud platform first; that's where current roles actually live.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;How fast is the big data job market growing?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;The global market is projected to go from $447.68 billion in 2026 to $1,176.57 billion by 2034, with related roles growing an estimated 23% or so per year.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Are remote big data engineering jobs available for freshers?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Yes — remote and hybrid roles are common at tech and product companies. Just know that with a bigger applicant pool, a documented portfolio project isn't optional anymore.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Which programming language matters most for big data roles?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Python, mostly because of how widely PySpark is used. That said, SQL is just as non-negotiable — nearly every role expects both.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;What is the difference between a data engineer and a big data engineer?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;A data engineer builds pipelines generally; a big data engineer specializes in the distributed, high-volume side of that work using Hadoop, Spark, and cloud infrastructure. At mid-size companies, the two titles tend to blur together anyway.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;How long does it take to become job-ready after a big data course?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Most people get there in four to nine months, depending on how much programming they already knew going in. One deployed, well-documented project is usually what finally turns interviews into offers.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      &quot;@id&quot;: &quot;https://www.nidads.com/blog/big-data-course-2026#speakable&quot;,
