    {
      &quot;@id&quot;: &quot;https://www.nidads.com/blog/data-analytics-course-with-placement#faq&quot;,
      &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;FAQPage&quot;,
      &quot;mainEntity&quot;: [
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Is placement guaranteed after a data analytics course?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;No. Most programs offer placement assistance, not a guaranteed job. Outcome depends on learner performance, market conditions, and the strength of the provider's hiring network. Contractual job guarantees exist but are less common and typically cost more.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;What skills are required for data analytics?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Core skills include Excel, SQL, Python, statistics, and data visualization using Power BI or Tableau. Employers prioritize SQL querying ability and basic Python proficiency alongside a documented project portfolio.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;What is the average salary of a data analyst in India?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Entry-level salaries typically range from ₹2.5–6 LPA depending on city and skillset, rising to ₹10–25 LPA with 3–5+ years of experience. Metro cities generally pay 30–50% more than tier-2 cities for equivalent roles.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;How long does it take to become a data analyst?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Most structured courses run 3–6 months, followed by additional time for placement preparation and job search. Total time to a first offer depends on portfolio strength and prior background.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Are online data analytics courses with placement worth it?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Yes, provided the curriculum is project-based and placement outcomes are verifiable. Online formats offer flexibility and typically lower cost, but value depends on instructor quality and documented placement data rather than course format alone.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Is data analytics a good career in 2026?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Yes. Industry sources including NASSCOM and the World Economic Forum continue to list data and analytics roles among the fastest-growing globally, driven by enterprise adoption of data-driven decision-making.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;What is the difference between a data analyst and a business analyst?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;A data analyst focuses on extracting, cleaning, and visualizing data to answer specific questions. A business analyst applies similar data skills but centers on business process improvement, requirements gathering, and stakeholder strategy.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Can I learn data analytics without a coding background?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Yes, for entry-level roles. Excel and visualization tools like Power BI require no coding. SQL and Python involve a shallow learning curve and are typically taught from fundamentals in structured courses.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Which is more important for placement: certification or projects?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Projects. Employers evaluate applied skills through a portfolio of real, documented case studies more than the certificate itself. A certification without project evidence rarely converts to interview calls.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
